{title: Go to Dark Gethsemane}
{artist: James Montgomery}
{key: Em}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 66}

Verse 1
[Em]Go to dark Geth[B]sema[Em]ne, [Am]ye that feel the [B]tempter's power;
[Em]your Redeemer's [B]conflict [Em]see, [Am]watch with him one [B]bitter hour:
[G]turn not from his [D]griefs a[Em]way — [Am]learn of Jesus [B]Christ to [Em]pray.

Verse 2
[Em]Follow to the judgment [Am]hall, view the Lord of [B]Life arraigned;
[Em]O the [B]wormwood [Em]and [Am]the gall! O the pangs [B]His soul
[G]sustained! Shun not suff'ring, [D]shame, or loss; learn [Am]from Christ to [B]bear the [Em]cross.

Verse 3
[Em]Calv'ry's mournful mountain climb; [Am]there, adoring at [B]His feet,
[Em]Mark that [B]miracle [Em]of [Am]time, God's own [B]sacrifice complete.
[G]"It is finished!" hear [D]Him cry; [Am]learn from Jesus [B]Christ to [Em]die.

Verse 4
[Em]Early hasten to the [Am]tomb where they laid His [B]breathless clay;
[Em]All is [B]solitude [Em]and [Am]gloom. Who has taken [B]Him away?
[G]Christ is ris'n! He [D]meets our eyes; [Am]Savior, teach us [B]so to [Em]rise.
